The emitter current of \(Q_{1}\) is given as \[I_{E1}=50\,\text{mA}\] Using \[I_{E}=(\beta+1)I_{B}\] for transistor \(Q_{1}\), \[I_{B1}=\frac{I_{E1}}{\beta_{1}+1}
=\frac{50\,\text{mA}}{99+1}
=0.5\,\text{mA}\] Since the emitter of \(Q_{2}\) is directly connected to the base of \(Q_{1}\), \[I_{E2}=I_{B1}=0.5\,\text{mA}\] Again, \[I_{E2}=(\beta_{2}+1)I_{B2}\] Hence, \[I_{B2}
=\frac{0.5\,\text{mA}}{49+1}
=\frac{0.5}{50}\,\text{mA}
=0.01\,\text{mA}
=10\,\mu\text{A}\] \[\boxed{10}\]

